      "sequence_position": 10,
      "problem": "Let $r=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]$ and $s=[\\begin{aligned}-15 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 25 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}].$ Find $3r+\\frac{1}{5}s.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we multiply each component of $r$ by $3$ and each component of $s$ by $\\frac{1}{5}.$ Then, we add the vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3r+\\frac{1}{5}s & =3\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-15 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 25 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 12 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9-3 \\\\ -3+0 \\\\ 6+5 \\\\ 12+0 \\\\ -12+2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 11 \\\\ 12 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
